  {"date": "2023-02-23", "venue": "Moon Palace", "city": "Cancun", "state": "Quintana Roo", "gap": 15, "set": "1", "prev": "Back on the Train", "in": "->", "next": "Sand"},
  {"date": "2023-04-14", "venue": "Climate Pledge Arena", "city": "Seattle", "state": "WA", "gap": 3, "set": "1", "note": "No \"Myfe\" ending.", "out": ">", "prev": "Steam", "in": ">", "next": "Walls of the Cave"},
  {"date": "2023-07-14", "venue": "Ameris Bank Amphitheatre", "city": "Alpharetta", "state": "GA", "gap": 9, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Maintaining a nice line that develops during the song's outro, discordant, near cacophonous and quite percussive play drives fluid Trey, whose dark soloing would sound at home in a recent \"Melt\" or atop a tower.", "note": "No \"Myfe\" ending.", "out": ">", "prev": "...And Flew Away", "next": "First Tube"},
  {"date": "2023-07-30", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 11, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "No clever ruse, \"MFMF\" goes big again, Trey working the song's melodic outro into a dark, driving solo; this is impassioned jamming that, in spots, sounds like \"Fuego.\" Fire play, either way, that, incredibly, sees Page jumping from his piano to his keys before -> for \"Gin\" and, of course, a return to his piano.", "note": "No \"Myfe\" ending.", "out": "->", "prev": "AC/DC Bag", "in": "->", "next": "Bathtub Gin"},
  {"date": "2023-10-11", "venue": "Ervin J. Nutter Center, Wright State University", "city": "Dayton", "state": "OH", "gap": 14, "set": "1", "note": "No \"Myfe\" ending.", "out": ">", "prev": "Steam", "in": ">", "next": "Crazy Sometimes"},
  {"date": "2023-12-29", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "A spirited version in its own right, Trey's vocal incantations (and power chords) build into a blistering \"heavy metal\" jam capped with a ferocious, percussive outro; here's swagger that winds down to inform an uncanny groove - like a series of handstands in grand fashion. -> into \"Sand\".", "note": "No \"Myfe\" ending.", "out": "->", "prev": "What's the Use?", "in": "->", "next": "Sand"},
  {"date": "2024-04-18", "venue": "Sphere", "city": "Las Vegas", "state": "NV", "gap": 6, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "-> from an old-school \"Tweezer\" outro (the true highlight, here), Trey once again >'s from \"MFMF\" to lead the band through a winding, droning passage of pleasant, somewhat discordant doom rock.", "note": "No \"Myfe\" ending.", "out": ">", "prev": "Tweezer", "in": "->", "next": "Mike's Song"},
  {"date": "2024-07-26", "venue": "Alpine Valley Music Theatre", "city": "East Troy", "state": "WI", "gap": 8, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Spoiler: No \"Myfe\" ending. Instead, we are again spoiled as Trey pushes the band into extended, driving, and impressively focused improvisation. If this is \"new norm,\" this version is arguably the most direct, with terrific intraband play well through the 11:00 mark. Here, play brightens, but eschews \"bliss\" in favor of more melodic, note-driven ideas, underscored by a terrific percussion rinse and play from Page on his concert grand. Jam peaks, but it's more in the form of a welcome release, and a huge blast of sustain; this cools to set up a wonderful \"Brian and Robert.\"", "note": "No \"Myfe\" ending.", "out": "->", "prev": "The Well", "next": "Brian and Robert"},
  {"date": "2024-08-09", "venue": "Bethel Woods Center for the Arts", "city": "Bethel", "state": "NY", "gap": 9, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Atoning for a somewhat ugly composed section, Trey slashes his way through a jam ignited by near full-band \"Fuego\" teasing, the four then yielding to a cool idea come 8:45, which builds to scattershot, yet engaging and musical improvisation, Trey finally finding a fun, atonal line before turning all \"Crosseyed and Painless,\" which, bettered by Page on his piano, leads to raucous improv, all of this building to inform a fun, playful, 'What the hell was that?' conclusion. Maybe so? Why not.", "note": "No \"Myfe\" ending.", "prev": "Cavern", "next": "Bug"},
  {"date": "2024-08-16", "venue": "The Woodlands", "city": "Dover", "state": "DE", "gap": 3, "set": "2", "note": "No \"Myfe\" ending.", "out": ">", "next": "No Men In No Man's Land"},
  {"date": "2024-09-01", "venue": "Dick's Sporting Goods Park", "city": "Commerce City", "state": "CO", "gap": 5, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Another \"MFMF,\" another huge, exploratory excursion. Out from a screaming vocal section, the band quickly locks into a groove that, while certainly marked by distinct, excellent segments (including, after the 12:00 minute mark, a bit by way of melody akin to the set-closing \"LSG\"), runs for a seamless near-twenty minutes > an extended, whimsical, vocal refrain.", "note": "No \"Myfe\" ending.", "prev": "The Moma Dance", "in": ">", "next": "Tube"},
  {"date": "2024-10-27", "venue": "MVP Arena", "city": "Albany", "state": "NY", "gap": 2, "set": "1", "note": "No \"Myfe\" ending.", "prev": "Access Me", "next": "My Sweet One"},
  {"date": "2024-12-31", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 3, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "After a generous helping of the aggressive murk we've perhaps come to expect from recent plays, the jam cools slightly and settles into an atypically groove laden space that pulses with hypnotic energy and drive, eventually sharpening on the edge of Trey's incisive riffing and concluding with a vocal reprise in lieu of the \"myfe\" ending.", "note": "No \"Myfe\" ending.", "out": ">", "prev": "Sigma Oasis", "in": ">", "next": "Sand"},
