  {"date": "2025-07-15", "venue": "TD Pavilion at the Mann", "city": "Philadelphia", "state": "PA", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "From the onset, this inspired exploration finds itself in a murky subterranean landscape, with thick, churning (but melodic) play from Mike and Trey. This remains the identity of the jam until about 2/3 in, when a break towards an infectiously catchy and upbeat theme via Page and Trey occurs. This rides delightfully toward a peak before receding towards a playful, vocal \"MYFE\" ending.", "prev": "Sand", "next": "Boogie On Reggae Woman"},
  {"date": "2025-07-26", "venue": "Broadview Stage at SPAC", "city": "Saratoga Springs", "state": "NY", "gap": 7, "set": "1", "out": ">", "prev": "Evolve", "next": "No Men In No Man's Land"},
  {"date": "2025-09-19", "venue": "Hampton Coliseum", "city": "Hampton", "state": "VA", "gap": 6, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Takes its time rumbling in the aftermath of the standard outro and then gradually winds up into a fairly intense vortex, then flips the tonality from minor to major in expectation of a peak but instead dwindles mysteriously > \"Rift\".", "out": ">", "prev": "46 Days", "next": "Rift"},
  {"date": "2025-12-31", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 5, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Continuing what started in 2023, the band appended another latter-day jam to this NYE version of \"MFMF\". While not breaking new ground, the band keeps the energy high throughout until they rustle up a frenzied peak, before Trey starts screaming the chorus again.", "prev": "Waste", "next": "A Life Beyond The Dream"},
  {"date": "2026-01-31", "venue": "Moon Palace", "city": "Cancun", "state": "Quintana Roo", "gap": 3, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "After a somewhat anemic and imperfect composed section, \"My Friend, My Friend\" launches into extended improvisation yet again. Grimy murk-rock takes center stage initially, before amorphously gliding into a more melodic, patient low key psychedelic rock passage. This then morphs into the final act: a patiently wound up, somewhat mellow bliss-rock segment with melodious, laser-tone Trey guitar peaks. Longest version to date.", "note": "No \"Myfe\" ending.", "prev": "Julius", "next": "Mull"},
